# 🤖 CARLOS

> CARLOS — Cost-efficient, Available, Replicated, Lightweight, Open, Secure — is an application architecture: one static Go binary per app, one fully-isolated instance per tenant (its own process and SQLite file), many instances on one small box, every database replicated to object storage and idle instances hibernating to it. This site documents the architecture, the platform that runs it, and the carlos CLI.

## Building a CARLOS app: start here

Everything an agent needs, in the order it is needed. The skills below carry the procedure; the rest is reference they point into.

1. [getting-started](https://carlosframework.com/.well-known/agent-skills/getting-started/SKILL.md): the recipe from an empty directory to a live URL, with the list of things only the person can do (Keymail identity, console sign-in, approving the CLI login, an amadan agent account and CI runner, DNS, anything billable). Read it first.
2. [building-carlos-apps](https://carlosframework.com/.well-known/agent-skills/building-carlos-apps/SKILL.md): for any app with more than one customer, team or person owning separate data. It starts with tenancy (what one instance is) and the trust class, then the platform, rastrillo and process references.
3. Rastrillo, the web framework. Its [SKILL.md](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rastrilloorg/rastrillo/main/SKILL.md) is the app story, read in full before writing code (mirror of amadan.net/rastrillo/rastrillo). [Topic docs](https://rastrillo.org/docs/), each page also served as markdown at /docs/<page>.md. Install: `go install amadan.net/rastrillo/rastrillo/cmd/rastrillo@latest` (Go 1.25+).
4. amadan, where the code lives. [House rules for agents](https://amadan.net/docs/-/agent-skill.md), or `amadan agent skill -install`; [getting started](https://amadan.net/docs/getting-started.md); [CI](https://amadan.net/docs/ci.md), which runs only once a runner serves the repo (runners are unsandboxed by default; getting-started says how to run one safely); [the CLI](https://amadan.net/docs/cli.md); [amadan's own llms.txt](https://amadan.net/llms.txt).
5. Carloku, the hosted platform. [The console](https://console.carloku.com). The `carlos` CLI: [binaries and checksums](https://github.com/carlosframework/releases), and [every command](https://carlosframework.com/docs/cli.md).
6. Trust classes, for declaring what the host can see: [the classes](https://carlosframework.com/trust/reference/).

